    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "ddc992979c89618f4259fcd0e05ae6c8",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Independent parameter check.</strong> Let\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\Delta(x)=xm^2-x(1-x)s-i0||)</marimo-tex> and\n$<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(L_0=\\int_0^1\\log\\frac{\\Delta(x)}{\\mu^2}\\,dx,\\qquad\nL_1=\\int_0^1(1-x)\\log\\frac{\\Delta(x)}{\\mu^2}\\,dx.||)</marimo-tex>$\nDirect parameter integration gives <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(V_f=-\\xi(1+2L_1)||)</marimo-tex> and\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(S_f=2+(3+\\xi)L_0||)</marimo-tex>. The quadrature splits at the internal root for\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(s&gt;m^2||)</marimo-tex>, retaining <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\log(-a-i0)=\\log a-i\\pi||)</marimo-tex>; the bubble then has positive\nimaginary part. At <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(s=0||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(s=m^2||)</marimo-tex>, exact parameter limits avoid a\nremovable zero or an endpoint singularity.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Near <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(s=0||)</marimo-tex>, separate double-precision evaluation of <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(A_0||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(B_0||)</marimo-tex> loses\naccuracy in their difference divided by <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(s||)</marimo-tex>. The comparison tolerance\naccounts for this conditioning, and the exact symbolic limit is used at zero.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "91d79fbc3b8702f97ef96a31a751fb1f",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The exact-<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(D||)</marimo-tex> check uses the Abelian limit of\n<a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0008171\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Davydychev, Osland and Saks</a>,\nEqs. (2.19)\u2013(2.21), with their gauge parameter <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\xi_{\\rm paper}=1-\\xi||)</marimo-tex>.\nAppendix C.6 provides a separate analytic check of the scalar bubble.\nThe <a href=\"https://feyncalc.github.io/FeynCalcExamples/QED/OneLoop/Renormalization2\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">FeynCalc QED example</a>\ndisplays the massive electron self-energy and then extracts its UV part;\nthe notebook here retains its finite coefficient as well.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Generation, tensor algebra, integral families, IBP and scalar master evaluation\nall use the shared components. The parameter integral above is an independent\ncheck, not a second master-integral evaluator in the Feynkit API.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    }
  ]
